<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>About — {{ site_title }}</title>
<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="./favicon.svg?v={{ asset_v['favicon.svg'] }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="./style.css?v={{ asset_v['style.css'] }}">
</head>
<body>
<header class="masthead">
  <div><h1><a href="./index.html">{{ site_title }}</a> / about</h1></div>
  <nav>
    <a href="./index.html">Table</a>
    <a href="./search.html">Search</a>
    {% if has_analysis %}<a href="./analysis.html">Analysis</a>{% endif %}
    {% if gh_repo %}<a href="https://github.com/{{ gh_repo }}">GitHub</a>{% endif %}
  </nav>
</header>

<article class="doc about">
  <p>{{ site_title }} is a public index of AI model documentation: model cards,
  system cards, and independent evaluation reports.</p>

  <h3>What it does</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Catalogs documents from an allowlist of AI labs and independent evaluators.</li>
    <li>Links the original of every document, and keeps an archived copy of every
        version it has captured{% if archive_base %}, downloadable from each document's
        version history{% endif %}.</li>
    <li>Fingerprints every document daily. Silent edits become recorded versions.</li>
    <li>Shows provenance for every entry: when, how, and why it was added.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>How it works</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>A deterministic monitor checks every link daily, re-fetches a rotating subset,
        and diffs publisher index pages for new documents.</li>
    <li>An LLM agent triages candidates and proposes entries. A deterministic validator
        (allowlist, fetchability, dedup, caps) has the final say on every write.</li>
    <li>The database is public SQLite{% if gh_repo %} in the
        <a href="https://github.com/{{ gh_repo }}">GitHub repo</a>{% endif %};
        this site is a static export of it.</li>
  </ul>

  {% if archive_base %}
  <h3>Archive and data</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Every captured version is archived byte for byte and named by its SHA-256, so
        anyone can verify a copy. Edits and removals stay checkable after the
        publisher changes the page.</li>
    <li>Download everything: <a href="{{ archive_base }}/cardtrack-dataset.tar.gz">the
        dataset</a> (database, extracted text, manifest), the
        <a href="{{ archive_base }}/manifest.json">manifest</a> of every version with its
        hash and link, and <code>wget -i {{ archive_base }}/urls.txt</code> for all originals.</li>
    <li>Archived copies are of publicly released documents; rights remain with their
        publishers. To request removal of a copy, write to
        {% if archive_contact %}<a href="mailto:{{ archive_contact }}">{{ archive_contact }}</a>{% else %}the maintainers{% endif %}.</li>
  </ul>
  {% endif %}

  <h3>Corrections</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Wrong entry: use the "report an issue" link on its page.</li>
    {% if gh_repo %}
    <li>Missing document:
      <a href="https://github.com/{{ gh_repo }}/issues/new?labels=missing-doc&title=%5Bmissing-doc%5D">file an issue</a>.</li>
    {% endif %}
  </ul>
</article>

<footer><p>Data updated {{ generated_at }}</p></footer>
</body>
</html>
